      "Language": "hrv",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To evaluate primary (technical) success and procedure safety in ultrasound (US)-guided percutaneous sclerotherapy of simple renal cysts, using 96% ethanol."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PATIENTS",
          "content": "17 patients with symptomatic simple renal cysts referred by nephrologists or urologists."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "US-guided percutaneous puncture of the cyst with an 18G (gauge) needle and a \"pigtail\" 5F (French) catheter, drainage and inspection of the cyst content, and injection of ethanol."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Puncture was rejected in two referred patients because of Bosniak II cyst and renal hilum proximity. 15 patients underwent puncture and drainage of the cyst content. In 4 patients ethanol was not injected because: thick or bloody cyst, proximity of renal hilum and severe pain during injection of ethanol. 11 patients underwent sclerotherapy of the cyst. The average size of sclerosed cyst was 8 cm (range 6-12 cm). There were no significant complications."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "US-guided percutaneous sclerotherapy of simple renal cysts is easy to perform and safe procedure, with the previous good selection of cysts that are suitable for the sclerotherapy."
        }
      ]},
